web: read extension resources from the page's own origin when it is not served over http(s)

The web workbench reads the resources of its built-in extensions (themes, grammars, snippets, language configurations) from the origin
that serves it: FileAccess.asBrowserUri() turns them into URLs under _VSCODE_FILE_ROOT, and the extension service registers a
fetch-backed, read-only file system provider (FetchFileSystemProvider) so that the file service can read them. It registers that provider
for http and https only. A workbench served from another scheme, an embedder's own protocol (a custom protocol of an Electron host, here
the vmapp-ui:// scheme of a vmapp window), gets `ENOPRO: No file system provider found` for every one of those resources: the default
color theme fails to load and no built-in grammar, snippet or language configuration is read.

This registers the same provider for the page's own scheme when it is neither http nor https and no provider exists for it yet. The
resources are then fetched from the page's origin exactly as they are over http(s). Nothing changes for a page served over http(s).

--- a/src/vs/workbench/services/extensions/browser/extensionService.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/services/extensions/browser/extensionService.ts
@@ -116,6 +116,13 @@
 		const provider = new FetchFileSystemProvider();
 		this._register(this._fileService.registerProvider(Schemas.http, provider));
 		this._register(this._fileService.registerProvider(Schemas.https, provider));
+
+		// A workbench served from another scheme than http(s) (an embedder's own protocol) reads the resources of its built-in
+		// extensions from its own origin as well.
+		const pageScheme = mainWindow.location.protocol.replace(/:$/, '');
+		if (pageScheme !== Schemas.http && pageScheme !== Schemas.https && !this._fileService.getProvider(pageScheme)) {
+			this._register(this._fileService.registerProvider(pageScheme, provider));
+		}
 	}

 	protected override async _initialize(): Promise<void> {
